<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">list</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">list</ansi> command lists items for sale at any merchants you are
visiting. Some merchants may even offer help for hire!

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">list</ansi>
  This would list whatever the merchant is carrying.

A shop that buys from players also lists, below its own goods, a table
of <ansi fg="cyan">Secondhand goods</ansi>: improved gear (a Keen, Warding, Empowered
or Masterwork piece) and trinkets of some worth that it bought from
players and will sell again. Each is one of a kind. Plain gear you sell
does not go there; it joins the shop's own goods like any other stock.
Cheap trinkets are not resold at all.

Find out more about referring to items by name by typing
<ansi fg="command">help item-names</ansi>.
